{
  "id": "u15-l02",
  "unit": "u15-describing",
  "title": "What are they like?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Character works like looks:** person + adjective, no verb. **ও কেমন মানুষ?** 'What kind of person is he?' **উনি খুব ভালো মানুষ** 'He's a really good person' is the everyday praise.\n\n**মজার** is U4's 'tasty'; about people it means funny: **মজার মানুষ**. **রাগী** 'short-tempered' comes from **রাগ** 'anger'.\n\nAge: **কম বয়সী** 'young' (literally 'of little age'). **বুড়ো** 'old' is blunt; **বয়স্ক** 'elderly' is the polite word, especially for someone you call আপনি. 'Isn't' after an adjective is just **না**: **ও বুড়ো না**.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "buro",
      "bn": "বুড়ো",
      "tr": "buro",
      "en": "old (of people)",
      "notes": "Plain, a little blunt; বয়স্ক is the polite word. For things, old is পুরনো."
    },
    {
      "id": "boyoshko",
      "bn": "বয়স্ক",
      "tr": "boyoshko",
      "en": "elderly",
      "notes": "The polite way to say 'old' about a person: উনি একজন বয়স্ক মানুষ."
    },
    {
      "id": "kom-boyoshi",
      "bn": "কম বয়সী",
      "tr": "kom boyoshi",
      "en": "young",
      "notes": "Literally 'of little age' (কম 'less' + বয়সী 'aged'). Small children are simply ছোট."
    },
    {
      "id": "bhalo-manush",
      "bn": "ভালো মানুষ",
      "tr": "bhalo manush",
      "en": "a good person; kind",
      "notes": "The everyday praise for someone's character: উনি খুব ভালো মানুষ."
    },
    {
      "id": "ragi",
      "bn": "রাগী",
      "tr": "ragi",
      "en": "short-tempered",
      "notes": "রাগ 'anger' (U14) + -ী: a person who gets angry easily. 'Angry right now' is আমার রাগ লাগছে."
    },
    {
      "id": "mojar-funny",
      "bn": "মজার",
      "tr": "mojar",
      "en": "funny",
      "notes": "About people: মজার মানুষ 'a funny person'. The same word means 'tasty' about food (U4: মজার খাবার)."
    },
    {
      "id": "lajuk",
      "bn": "লাজুক",
      "tr": "lajuk",
      "en": "shy"
    },
    {
      "id": "hashikhushi",
      "bn": "হাসিখুশি",
      "tr": "hashikhushi",
      "en": "cheerful",
      "notes": "হাসি 'smile' + খুশি 'happy': someone who is always cheerful. খুশি alone is how you feel now."
    }
  ],
